From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:57:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D104 attachments: notes that replace or label an attachment
 start their own paragraph
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream: when a model cannot read an attachment, its media part is replaced by a text part ("ERROR: Cannot read …"), and a local image or PDF is preceded by an "Attached file: <path>" text part. Neither starts with a separator, and OpenAI-compatible chat requests join a user message's text parts, so the model received "Read theseERROR: Cannot read …" and "…Attached file: /path…" glued to the prompt. Text and directory attachments already start with a blank line for this reason.
Fixed: both start with a blank line, like text attachments ("Read these\n\nERROR: Cannot read …"). Tool-result replacements are unchanged (their text items are joined with newlines).
Scenarios: session-api-inputs.test.ts "attachments the model cannot read", "prompt with file and agent attachments"; agent-loop-agents.test.ts "prompt with a PDF attachment", "prompt with image attachments"; tui nav-paste.test.ts "paste a file path attaches the file" (re-recorded request text)
Upstream tests: test/session-model-request.test.ts and test/session-runner-message.test.ts (asserted the unseparated text), test/session-compaction.test.ts (token estimates grow by one per replaced attachment)

diff --git a/packages/core/src/session/model-request.ts b/packages/core/src/session/model-request.ts
index b218f6f47d..5fc93d8032 100644
--- a/packages/core/src/session/model-request.ts
+++ b/packages/core/src/session/model-request.ts
@@ -167,9 +167,10 @@ const replaceMedia = (
   messages: LLMRequest["messages"],
   replace: (media: { mime: string; name: string | undefined; bytes: () => number }) => string | undefined,
 ) => {
+  // Providers may join a message's text parts, so the replacement starts its own paragraph like text attachments.
   const media = (part: MediaPart) => {
     const text = replace({ mime: part.media.mediaType, name: part.filename, bytes: () => mediaBytes(part.media) })
-    return text === undefined ? part : Message.text(text)
+    return text === undefined ? part : Message.text(`\n\n${text}`)
   }
   const toolResult = (part: ToolResultPart) => {
     if (part.result.type !== "content") return part
diff --git a/packages/core/src/session/runner/to-llm-message.ts b/packages/core/src/session/runner/to-llm-message.ts
index 47c6fc4a14..db80374b4c 100644
--- a/packages/core/src/session/runner/to-llm-message.ts
+++ b/packages/core/src/session/runner/to-llm-message.ts
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@ const attachmentContent = (file: FileAttachment): Array<TextPart | MediaPart> =>
   if (file.mime === "application/x-directory") return [directoryAttachment(file)]
   if (imageMimes.has(file.mime) || file.mime === "application/pdf") {
     const location = attachmentLocation(file)
-    return [...(location === undefined ? [] : [Message.text(`Attached file: ${location}`)]), media(file)]
+    return [...(location === undefined ? [] : [Message.text(`\n\nAttached file: ${location}`)]), media(file)]
   }
   return []
 }
